  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 520.06 Renewal of Walking Disability Plates and Placards",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 520.06 Renewal of Walking Disability Plates and Placards.\n\n(a) Walking disability plates shall be renewed in accordance with the requirements of Saf-C 511.\n\n(b) Each person who has a walking disability plate or walking disability vanity plate shall submit a form RDMV 130 (rev.8/21) to the department during the month of the applicant’s registration renewal every 5 years.\n\n(c) Walking disability placards shall be valid for 5 years from the person’s date of birth, or, if an organization, during the organization’s month of renewal set forth in Saf-C 510.08.\n\n(d) Each person who has a permanent walking disability placard shall submit form RDMV 130 (rev.8/21) to the department during the month of the person’s date of birth every 5 years.\n\nSource. #7069, eff 8-5-99 (formerly Saf-C 518, see Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 500); ss by #8999, eff 9-29-07; ss by #10135, eff 5-23-12; ss by #13521, eff 1-13-23 (formerly Saf-C 521.07)",
